<title>OMAN: Oman names BP Chemicals in petrochems jv.</title>
<headline>Oman names BP Chemicals in petrochems jv.</headline>
<dateline>MUSCAT 1996-11-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oman said on Sunday it had appointed BP Chemicals -- a unit of British Petroleum -- as its partner in a $900 million petrochemical complex to produce 450,000 tonnes a year of ethylene and polyethylene.</p>
<p>The official Oman News Agency quoted Minister of Commerce and Industry Makboul bin Ali Bin Sultan as saying the complex would start production by the year 2000.</p>
<p>Teams would meet from Monday to discuss details of setting up the project, which he said was a very important part of the sultanate's industrial strategy.</p>
</text>
